# Sources: Ervand Abrahamian, Iran Between Two Revolutions,
# ch. 5, pp. 250–267; official Majles proceedings, session 25, 18 May 1950.
# Mechanical effects are counterfactual abstractions.
title: <span class="term term-constitutionalist">Allahyar Saleh</span>
new-page: true
is-pinned-card: true
tags: advisor
view-if: advisor_saleh_available = 1 and advisor_saleh_active = 1

= {!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Allahyar Saleh{!</span>!}

{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Saleh{!</span>!} works through
the {!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!}'s
electoral and organizational machinery. His consultation concentrates on
durable local committees and records that can withstand public or
parliamentary scrutiny.

- @saleh_reports
- @saleh_committee
- @saleh_credentials
- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@saleh_reports
title: Audit constituency reports
subtitle: <span class="term term-constitutionalist">Saleh</span> separates claims that can survive a credential hearing from rumor that cannot
view-if: parliamentary_deck_unlocked = 1
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and parliamentary_deck_unlocked = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 6;
Q.electoral_committee_timer = 0;
Q.parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 4;
Q.organizational_reach += 2;
for (var place of Q.majles_places) {
    if (place.scenario.contestable) place.scenario.legal_defense += 4;
}
!}

{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Saleh{!</span>!} reviews
constituency reports against
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!} records
and asks organizers to label observation, hearsay, and missing evidence
separately. Uncertain returns remain uncertain.

Party organizers gain a record they can use in election complaints and later
credential petitions without overstating uncertain evidence.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@saleh_committee
title: Strengthen local committees
subtitle: Local <span class="term term-constitutionalist">Iran Party</span> committees collect complaints, names, and returns in a common form
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; membership_committees_timer = 0; organizational_reach += 4; iran_party_organization += 3; support_provincial += 2

{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Saleh{!</span>!} works through
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!} contacts
to standardize meeting records,
membership follow-up, and reports to the party office. The committees remain
locally rooted while becoming easier to connect beyond one constituency.

[? if front_formed = 0: The party reaches farther and receives more regular
reports from its own contacts. ?]
[? if front_formed = 1: The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!}
reaches farther through one component's machinery and receives more regular
reports from those contacts. ?]

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@saleh_credentials
title: Prepare a model credential file
subtitle: One exemplary file becomes a model other deputies can carry into the chamber
view-if: majles_convened = 1
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and majles_convened = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; credential_petitions_timer = 0; parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 4; mossadegh_authority += 1; iran_party_relation += 2

{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Saleh{!</span>!} assembles one complete file that distinguishes the return, the credential
decision, and the point at which a deputy becomes usable in the chamber. The
format gives other organizers a standard they can copy.

The credential campaign becomes more disciplined and
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!} cooperation
improves. One model cannot resolve every disputed place.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing
